<title>USA: CBOT March volume rises 8.3 pct yr/yr to 19.9 mln.</title>
<headline>CBOT March volume rises 8.3 pct yr/yr to 19.9 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said the trading volume in its futures and options totalled 19,939,172 contracts in March, up 8.3 percent from 18,404,486 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for March 1997 and percentage change followed by March 1996 volume:</p>
<p>All futures     15,633,539     + 7.8     14,504,636</p>
<p>  Agricultural   4,534,265     +15.4	3,928,293</p>
<p>  Financial     11,094,484     + 5.0     10,569,217</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   4,305,633     +10.4	3,899,850</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,209,809     +26.0	  959,963</p>
<p>  Financial	3,094,478     + 5.3	2,939,541</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     7,493,261     + 4.1	7,199,252</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 2,051,797     - 1.2	2,075,770</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes  1,271,135     +17.2	1,084,857</p>
<p>  Wheat		368,547     -19.2	  455,981</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,693,321     + 5.3	1,607,555</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,405,906     +39.3	1,009,372</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    509,512     +16.9	  435,764</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     503,998     +34.3	  375,237</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,450,506     +31.5	1,862,906</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   443,203     -43.6	  785,301</p>
<p>  Corn		 443,495     - 7.5	  479,531</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   522,855     +59.5	  327,801</p>
<p>((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750/E-mail:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
